Hello Kafka committers and contributors.

As you know - next week we have the flagship Community Over Code conference
in Denver and together with Isma=C3=ABl we are co-charing data engineering =
track.

There are many parallel tracks in Denver, but Data Engineering is held on
Wednesday and Thursday in Mt. Wilson - you can check all that here
https://communityovercode.org/schedule/

There are interesting talks and we planned the track carefully to have
really interesting talks - starting from a general overview of the data
engineering landscape and going into details of some of the Data
Engineering toolbox.

I am also quite happy to tell you that this year we have the "security"
topic - which is pretty much across-all-projects presented by me on
Wednesday at 4:50 pm.

This is not only very close to my "Security committee member" heart, but I
want to share some insights of a project we run with Alpha-Omega "Airflow
Beach cleaning" - which is all about improving security of the whole supply
chain of Airflow. That is an experimental project we run and I would like
to get your feedback, suggestion and brainstorming on it as well as enthuse
others to start thinking if they could do a similar approach. The talk will
be followed by a Birds of a Feather session on the topic, so we should have
plenty of time for interaction.

We are looking forward to meeting you next week in Denver!

J.

