Subject: RE: [DISCUSS] KIP-1093: Add more observability for MirrorMaker2
Message-Id: <836C46DA-B9F6-46B7-BF03-EF375E129642@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Oct 2024 18:03:26 +0800
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
X-Mailer: Apple Mail (2.3774.400.31)

Thank you for your insights on Kafka MirrorMaker2's observability. In =
addition to your proposed metrics, I'm wondering if there are plans to =
include a metric for replication delay. This could provide vital =
information about the number of messages yet to be replicated, similar =
to consumer lag. Could you share your thoughts on this?


On 2024/09/23 10:00:01 Frank Yang wrote:
> Hi everyone,
>=20
> I=E2=80=99d like to kick off the discussion of new metrics in =
MirrorMaker2.
>=20
> =
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1093%3A+Add+more+obs=
ervability+for+MirrorMaker2
>=20
> Feel free to give me any suggestion and feedback. Thanks for your =
review.
>=20
> Thanks,
> PoAn
>=20
>=20
>=20=

