    Resolution: Fixed

> Remove deprecated Consumer API poll(long timeout)
> -------------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-15908
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15908
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Sub-task
>          Components: clients, consumer
>            Reporter: Kirk True
>            Assignee: Andrew Schofield
>            Priority: Critical
>              Labels: consumer-threading-refactor, timeout
>             Fix For: 4.0.0
>
>
> Per [KIP-266|https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-266%3A+Fix+consumer+indefinite+blocking+behavior], the {{Consumer.poll(long timeout)}} method was deprecated back in 2.0.0. 
> In 3.7, there are two implementations, each with different behavior:
> * The {{LegacyKafkaConsumer}} implementation will continue to work but will log a warning about its removal
> * The {{AsyncKafkaConsumer}} implementation will throw an error.
> In 4.0, the `poll` method that takes a single `long` timeout will be removed altogether.



