Hi Christo,

Thanks for the KIP!

I had some thoughts that are relevant to Kafka broker out-of-space
conditions, and I'll offer them here to see if they make sense to
incorporate into this KIP, or if someone suggested them before.

1. Rather than respond to an out-of-disk condition after it has happened,
provide mechanisms to monitor and respond to disk utilization at all times.
As the disk utilization increases, prioritize operations which reduce it
(deletion/compaction/archive) and deprioritize operations which increase it
(produce to leader, fetching remote segments).
This can provide a soft-degradation of a broker as disks become full, and
could cause a broker to reach a steady-state disk utilization rather than
running full speed until failure.

2. For clusters with tiered storage, trigger segment rolling earlier than
specified in the topic configuration when disk utilization is high. This
could allow a tiered-storage broker to support topics with a total segment
size larger than the provisioned disk capacity, without risking that all
segments being almost-full causes an out-of-space condition.

Thanks,
Greg

