Anton Agestam created KAFKA-17845:
-------------------------------------

             Summary: UpdateRaftVoterResponse has incorrect default value f=
allbacks
                 Key: KAFKA-17845
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17845
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
    Affects Versions: 3.9.0
            Reporter: Anton Agestam


This was discovered through property testing for upgrading kio to Kafka 3.9=
.0-rc2 schema.

We have tests in place to assert that our protocol serializer implementatio=
n is sync with upstream Kafka.

The test discovered a discrepancy between kio and Kafka for this instance:

=C2=A0
{code:java}
E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 instance=3DUpdateRaftVoterResponse(
E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 throttle_time=3Ddatetime=
.timedelta(0),
E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 error_code=3D<ErrorCode.=
unknown_server_error: -1>,
E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 current_leader=3DCurrent=
Leader(
E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 leader_id=
=3D-1,
E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 leader_epo=
ch=3D-1,
E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 host=3D'',
E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 port=3D0,
E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 ),
E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 ), {code}
kio serializes this as `"AAAAAP//AQAO//////////8BAAAAAAA=3D"` while Kafka s=
erializes it as `"AAAAAP//AA=3D=3D"` (base 64 encoded bytes).

This is as if the `host` and `port` fields have defaults of empty string an=
d zero, but they do not.=C2=A0

This looks to me like the behavior for [deserializing a message from a prev=
ious version=C2=A0|https://github.com/apache/kafka/tree/trunk/clients/src/m=
ain/resources/common/message#deserializing-messages] is incorrectly kicking=
 in here.

I would expect to either see the defaults declared in the schema, or for th=
is model to not exercise this "omit the nested entity" behavior at all, sin=
ce all of the fields of the nested entity do not have default values.

=C2=A0



