    Resolution: Invalid

> UpdateRaftVoterResponse has incorrect default value fallbacks
> -------------------------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-17845
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17845
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Bug
>    Affects Versions: 3.9.0
>            Reporter: Anton Agestam
>            Priority: Major
>
> This was discovered through property testing for upgrading kio to Kafka 3=
.9.0-rc2 schema.
> We have tests in place to assert that our protocol serializer implementat=
ion is sync with upstream Kafka.
> The test discovered a discrepancy between kio and Kafka for this instance=
:
> =C2=A0
> {code:java}
> E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 instance=3DUpdateRaftVoterResponse(
> E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 throttle_time=3Ddateti=
me.timedelta(0),
> E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 error_code=3D<ErrorCod=
e.unknown_server_error: -1>,
> E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 current_leader=3DCurre=
ntLeader(
> E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 leader_i=
d=3D-1,
> E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 leader_e=
poch=3D-1,
> E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 host=3D'=
',
> E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 port=3D0=
,
> E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 ),
> E =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 ), {code}
> kio serializes this as `"AAAAAP//AQAO//////////8BAAAAAAA=3D"` while Kafka=
 serializes it as `"AAAAAP//AA=3D=3D"` (base 64 encoded bytes).
> This is as if the `host` and `port` fields have defaults of empty string =
and zero, but they do not.=C2=A0
> This looks to me like the behavior for [deserializing a message from a pr=
evious version=C2=A0|https://github.com/apache/kafka/tree/trunk/clients/src=
/main/resources/common/message#deserializing-messages] is incorrectly kicki=
ng in here.
> I would expect to either see the defaults declared in the schema, or for =
this model to not exercise this "omit the nested entity" behavior at all, s=
ince all of the fields of the nested entity do not have default values.
> =C2=A0



