Hi Pradyumna,=0A=
Yes, you can do this. What I tend to do is to start my broker from a termin=
al window with the=0A=
DEBUG_SUSPEND_FLAG and KAFKA_DEBUG environment variables set. This means th=
e broker=0A=
suspends as it starts and waits for a connection from a debugger. Then I at=
tach IntelliJ to the=0A=
running broker with my breakpoints set and I can use the debugger.=0A=
=0A=
So, my command line would be something like:=0A=
=0A=
DEBUG_SUSPEND_FLAG=3Dy KAFKA_DEBUG=3Dy bin/kafka-server-start.sh --bootstra=
p-server .....=0A=
=0A=
Hope this helps.=0A=
Andrew=0A=
