>> I noticed that some of the KIP-1022 work that was meant to make it in=
 this
>> release was removed.
>> Without any specifications, the cluster is meant to take the latest v=
ersion
>> of all available features. The code to do that was removed. Perhaps t=
here
>> is a reason, but we should either change the KIP or remedy this.
>> Not only that, but the ability to configure a feature via the --featu=
re
>> flag in the storage tool also seems to be removed but the text remain=
s when
>> running with no arguments. I don't think it is a blocker, but this sh=
ould
>> be fixed for 4.0.
>
> For kraft.version (aka KIP-853) we opted to have the formatting tool=20
> enable the feature automatically if controller.quorum.voter is not=20
> specified. In other words, if you configure a static quorum, the=20
> formatter gives you a static quorum; otherwise, the formatter creates =
a=20
> dynamic quorum. We felt that this was more intuitive than making the=20
> user manually supply --feature kraft.version=3D1 when dynamic quorums=20
> were in use, and --feature kraft.version=3D0 when static quorums were =
in=20
> use.
>
> Another issue is that if the formatter had automatically set everyone=20
> to dynamic quorums, it would have been an incompatible change.=20
> Configuration files without controller.quorum.bootstrap.servers can't=20
> be used when dynamic quorums are in use. I think people would have=20
> perceived this as "3.9 is broken" since their old configurations would=20
> have stopped working.
>
> Note that it may still be useful to specify --feature kraft.version=3D=
1=20
> since that will force the formatter to always give you a dynamic=20
> quorum, and error out if that is not possible.
>
