Greg Harris created KAFKA-17871:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: Source task source offset reads can block herder task=
 cancellation
                 Key: KAFKA-17871
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17871
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: connect
    Affects Versions: 2.5.0
            Reporter: Greg Harris


In KAFKA-9051, source task offsets reading was modified to allow for in-pro=
gress read Futures to be cancelled during task shutdown. The OffsetReaderSt=
orageImpl#offsetReadFutures uses explicitly synchronized accesses to preven=
t data races between task cancellation and connectors reading offsets.

A thread executing OffsetReaderStorageImpl#offsets method can lock the Set,=
 and then call Producer#flush inside KafkaBasedLog#flush.

At the same time, the herder thread may try to shut down the task, time out=
, and call AbstractWorkerSourceTask#cancel. This cancellation attempts to l=
ock the Set again, and must wait for the Producer#flush to complete. If the=
 task's producer is unhealthy, this can block the herder thread indefinitel=
y.

