Hi Anton,

The behavior where we leave out tagged fields when the default value is =
present is intentional. As is the behavior where default values are trea=
ted as 0, the empty array, etc. when defaults are not explicitly specifi=
ed. These two behaviors, taken together, save space on the wire, and are=
 simpler for us to implement than what you have proposed. You haven't pr=
esented a single reason why this should change.

There simply isn't any reason to change the current tagged fields behavi=
or. And even if we wanted to, it would require a KIP, whereas 3.9 is pas=
t KIP freeze (along with feature freeze, code freeze, and every other fr=
eeze.)

best,
Colin


