In all the cases I can remember, we actually wanted an invalid port and =
invalid hostname to be the default, so that we could clearly differentia=
te the case where a port and hostname were sent back from the case where=
 they were not. So in this particular case the implicit defaults are act=
ually exactly what we want.

If we wanted to get rid of implicit defaults and make everything explici=
t, we would have to introduce a richer syntax for initializing some type=
s, like UUIDs, collections, etc. Collections alone would be daunting sin=
ce the problem is recursive (I can have a collection containing other co=
llections, etc.)

