>              Labels: consumer-threading-refactor, kip-848-client-support
>             Fix For: 4.0.0
>
>
> There are still some calls to change the subscriptionState subscription i=
n the app thread, that could lead to race-conditions given that the subscri=
ption state object is shared between the background and app thread and is m=
ostly updated in the background. We should consider moving the subscription=
State.subscribe() and subscribeFromPattern calls to the background.
> [https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/5624bc7c7e43339eb64e18491ac5039324e=
50678/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/clients/consumer/internals/Asy=
ncKafkaConsumer.java#L1465]
> [https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/5624bc7c7e43339eb64e18491ac5039324e=
50678/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/clients/consumer/internals/Asy=
ncKafkaConsumer.java#L1703]
> [https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/5624bc7c7e43339eb64e18491ac5039324e=
50678/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/clients/consumer/internals/Asy=
ncKafkaConsumer.java#L1736]
> One option would be to use the existing SubscriptionChangeEvent, perform =
the subscription (and metadata) changes in the AppEventProcessor (where uns=
ubscribe already takes place).=C2=A0
> Note that these calls are closely related to metadata object calls, to re=
quest metadata for new topics and "maybeUpdateSubscriptionMetadata". We sho=
uld maybe consider moving them together to the background (where the metada=
ta object is also updated).=C2=A0 [https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/562=
4bc7c7e43339eb64e18491ac5039324e50678/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafk=
a/clients/consumer/internals/AsyncKafkaConsumer.java#L1703-L1705]=C2=A0



