Hi Daniel,



This would indeed greatly reduce the duplicate processing on failbacks.



Few questions:

   1. Since having a second offset-sync store can be memory intensive,
   would it make sense to filter the topics in it based on the
   reverseCheckpointingTopicFilter?
   2. Would it make sense to add a reverseCheckpointingGroupFilter as well,
   so that one can control not just the topics for reverse checkpointing bu=
t
   also the groups?



Do I understand this correctly, that the replication flow itself must be
bidirectional, but the topic replication doesn=E2=80=99t? If so, this seems=
 to
unlock another use case. With this change, one can more confidently fail
over the consumer group to the passive cluster and back (in the context of
the topic itself), without much reprocessing; I see this useful when a
cluster gets busy at times. Or even have a new consumer group consume
messages from the passive cluster for a while, before =E2=80=9Cfailing it o=
ver=E2=80=9D to
the active cluster. Is this something that you would recommend using the
feature for?



Best,

Vidor

